These seven old fragments are unique. The authored title is `00. 対象と設計の決定`, omitting the old title's 上; a title-based automatic anchor cannot be assumed compatible. All annotated headings contain Ruby readings in /2 display, so keep the old-anchor table explicit and inspect the new generated automatic IDs rather than copying Chapter 13's two-auto/six-alias decision. `result.json` also records the six distinct UTF-8-hex `n-` Section anchors. Old versus new automatic-anchor collisions have not been executed.

The source and draft have zero links, zero code blocks and zero tables. Both contain the same ten ordered InlineCode values: cons, nil, v1, Fn, value, splice, call, map, then, design/forms.json. `design/forms.json` is code text, not a typed resource link. The 14–16 chapter reference is also plain text. Thus moving this page introduces no relative links inside it that require rewriting. The inbound guide README links to `spec/00-contract.md`; retaining the logical projection path preserves that target. Repository scan found no explicit inbound `00-contract.md#fragment` link, but externally bookmarked old anchors remain part of compatibility.

The original Markdown has one six-item list. The manual draft has three nonempty flat unordered lists (4 language items, 6 semantic-boundary items, 14 invariant items), each with exactly one Paragraph per item. This is an intentional pre-existing authored structure, covered in earlier review; it is not an /2 renderer structural loss. It fits /2's current flat-list contract without adjacent independent lists, task states, nested items, tables or invented filler. Compare all 4/6/14 items, annotations and INV01–INV14 in the final view; do not require the old restricted fixture's exact Markdown event sequence for this authored view.

`design/doc-inventory.json` and `doc/history/source-manifest.json` include the original path/hash as baseline evidence. Their historical bytes must not be silently updated into current-success receipts. Any current migration/registry record must distinguish preserved baseline from the newly registered source. Existing review archives remain historical and should not be rewritten when the draft moves.

