`check.py` fixed the inputs, compared both to reviewed Git blobs, parsed complete Doc structure using existing formal forms, extracted exact InlineCode sequence and 4/6/14 list counts, verified absence of links/rawcode/table, and extracted seven anchors from actual GitHub server HTML. It retained the tracked-reference scan and original review records. This is not production parse/lower/render. Root reported current actual parse → annotated /2 success; I did not repeat or convert that report into independently executed evidence. New-view semantic review by a different author, actual GitHub/browser navigation, HTML accessibility, generated-byte determinism and full canonical check remain root's cutover gates. No broader T21 completion is claimed.
